# Build directories. One pattern for every separator the docs and CI use:
# `build/`, `build_gpu/`, and `build-gpu/` (the name INSTALL.md and the
# gpu-portable-isa CI job teach). The previous `build/` + `build_*/` pair
# missed the hyphen, so `build-gpu/` showed up as untracked in every status.
# Trailing slash: directories only, so scripts/build_lola_ring.py is untouched.
build*/
CMakeCache.txt
CMakeFiles/
cmake_install.cmake
Makefile

# Compiled object files
*.o
*.obj
*.so
*.dll
*.dylib
*.a

# Editor / IDE files
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Python packaging artifacts (pip install -e . writes the egg-info tree)
*.egg-info/
build/lib/
dist/

# Claude Code
.claude/
CLAUDE.md

# BFG cleanup artifacts
.git.backup/
..bfg-report/

# Generated data files
*.bin
*.fits
*.dat
output/
results/

# Large data — dataset CONTENTS are ignored (distributed via
# scripts/fetch_data.py + data/data_manifest.json), but the per-dataset
# provenance README.md files are tracked (hence the ** / !**/ / !README.md
# triplets). data/kernels is handled by data/kernels/.gitignore; data/spice
# (1.6 MB mission SPKs) is tracked.
data/maps/*.fits
data/meshes/moon3d_cartesian_double.ply
data/emission/
# fetch_data.py keeps the verified tarballs it downloaded (~1.4 GB after
# --core) so that --verify can re-hash them without re-downloading. Every
# unpack DESTINATION is ignored below, but this cache was not, leaving it the
# one thing `git status` reports after a documented data fetch.
data/_downloads/
data/dem/**
!data/dem/**/
!data/dem/**/README.md
data/topo/**
!data/topo/**/
!data/topo/**/README.md
data/property_maps/**
!data/property_maps/**/
!data/property_maps/**/README.md
data/albedo_maps/**
!data/albedo_maps/**/
!data/albedo_maps/**/README.md
data/external/**
!data/external/**/
!data/external/**/README.md
data/jwst/

# Local caches and outputs
.cache/
camera_output/
plots/
notebooks/
# ...except the tracked, executed tutorial notebooks (docs/tutorials/notebooks/
# is a deliberate onboarding path, not a scratch dir the "notebooks/" rule above
# was written for -- unanchored pattern, so it silently matched this path too).
!docs/tutorials/notebooks/
!docs/tutorials/notebooks/**
examples/data/
docs/figures/jwst/

# Research papers (keep locally, reference by DOI in docs)
docs/*.pdf

# Internal planning/optimization docs (not user-facing)
docs/RADIATION_EXCHANGE_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md
docs/HMATRIX_OPTIMIZATION_ROADMAP.md
docs/thermal-efficiency-plan.md
docs/gui-upgrade-plan.md
docs/Iterative_Spectral_Thermal_Model_Plan.md
docs/T-Dependent_Thermophysical_Properties_Implementation.md
docs/AVX-512_Hardware_Acceleration_for_ISM.md
docs/radiation_exchange_integration_plan.md
docs/Planetary\ Thermal\ Model\ Optimization.md
docs/SIMD\ Vectorization_\ Depth\ vs.\ Pixels.md
docs/SIMD\ Optimization\ Mismatch_\ Pixel\ vs.\ Depth.md
docs/GPU\ Radiosity\ Solver\ Feedback.md
docs/Optimizing\ Radiation\ Module\ Performance.md

# Backup files
*.backup
*.backup.*
*.bak
*-MacL4864*.cpp
*NOTWORKING*

# Archive folder
archive/

# External research modules
ext/

# Debug/test output
illumination_series.csv

# Serialized config format
*.ptm3d

# Example configs not tracked (keep only core examples)
examples/europa_high_res2.yaml
examples/moon_heatflow_high.yaml
examples/moon_heatflow_low.yaml
examples/haworth5m_heatflow_high.yaml
examples/haworth5m_heatflow_high_long.yaml
examples/haworth5m_heatflow_low.yaml
examples/leibniz_disco.yaml

# Raw Diviner seasonal ASCII grids (~1.6G; re-downloadable from
# luna1.diviner.ucla.edu/~jpierre/diviner/level4_polar/). Only the
# pre-filtered *_polar.npy (lat < -86.5) are tracked.
data/diviner_seasonal/*.txt

# Local scratch: working mesh copies (OneDrive evicts cloud placeholders for
# C++ readers, so meshes are re-pinned here) and ad-hoc dump files.
tmp/
tmp_illum_*.txt

# internal working notes — never ship
SESSION-NOTES-*.md
TASK-*.md
RUNBOOK-*.md
TICKET-*.md
